# Local eighteen role child readiness controls

Use check.py with a fresh fixed host, 194, 188 or metadata lane. Corrections use
distinct final lanes. Every lane is exclusive: first results cannot be overwritten.
The historical absence baseline cannot be rerun after the component exists.
Native commands use unprivileged local WSL and owned helper processes/files/FDs.
No original live manager attempt, service, clock, namespace, server, installation
or product workload is part of these controls.

The new child accepts only the exact activation environment and eighteen roles.
Its readiness exchange is one-shot and nonexecuting; guardian, creator, channel
events and the original absolute alarm end the hold. Real owned-child SIGKILL
and unconsumed ACK controls do not constitute the full original-start crash
matrix or proof of all-writer cessation. All 300/60/10 windows stay unchanged.

The logger retains source snapshots, exact argv, exits, stdout/stderr and hashes.
Test elapsed time is not a performance measurement or original-window-fit claim.
After committing the checked sources and retention method, retain.py requires
that exact commit and four successful lanes sharing the same source snapshot.
It checks every command and log, preserves earlier failures and pins the frozen
qualification digest. The resulting archive admits neither execution nor release.
